---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="LLM Provider Partnership — Value Vision"
  description="What the Poesis stack brings to LLM capabilities — and what LLMs bring to Poesis. Models propose; humans and Poesis dispose. The governed context layer that makes sovereign AI more capable and deployable."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Partnerships</p>
      <h1>LLM Provider Partnership — Value Vision.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Frontier models reason against statistical traces of the world — not against an explicit, causal, governed model of it. That single gap drives both of today's ceilings: the <a href="#capability-ceiling"><strong>capability ceiling</strong></a> and the <a href="#deployment-ceiling"><strong>deployment ceiling</strong></a>. Poesis closes both with one layer — and model providers are the natural partners on it.</p>
      <p class="lead"><strong>Models propose. Human &amp; Poesis dispose.</strong> Every model output is a proposal until humans, supported by the governed definition layer, validate it — deterministically and with an audit trail behind every disposition.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Talk to us</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/gsm">The GSM standard</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/sie">The SIE engine</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why partner</p>
      <h2>One substrate, two wins.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <div class="card card--feature" id="capability-ceiling">
          <span class="tag">Capability</span>
          <h3>It makes artificial intelligence more capable.</h3>
          <p>A model that trains and reasons against an explicit causal model — what affects what, through which mechanism, under which governing intent — works against <em>structure</em> rather than guessing from correlation. It can follow the why behind the why: trace impact, test counterfactuals, plan against real dependencies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature" id="deployment-ceiling">
          <span class="tag">Deployability</span>
          <h3>It makes artificial intelligence deployable.</h3>
          <p>The same governed model turns output into accountable action: governed context in, proposals out, deterministic disposition against Norms, schemas, and provenance — recorded in an append-only audit ledger. Agentic AI that regulated organisations can actually run.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The value flows</p>
      <h2>An interactive map of the exchange.</h2>

      <div id="vf">
        <div class="vf-notices" aria-label="How to read the value map">
          <p class="vf-notice vf-notice-info"><strong>Explore the map.</strong> Click a flow to see its mutual value. Click an LLM or Poesis component to see every adherence it has with the other components. Expand a Poesis box for internal detail.</p>
          <p class="vf-notice vf-notice-invariant"><strong>Core invariant:</strong> models <strong>PROPOSE</strong> (inferred, confidence &lt; 1.0) · humans dispose through ITIP · SIE enforces deterministically — <strong>PROPOSE / DISPOSE</strong>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-human">
          <strong>Human supervision, regulation, and governance — always in the loops.</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Owns Intents</b> — creation of Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
            <li><b>Owns Approvals</b> — validation of AI-proposed Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
            <li><b>Owns Accountability</b> — evaluation and simulation of Definition / Ascription compliance and impacts, and audit of AI and human actions over Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-diagram" id="vf-diagram">
          <svg id="vf-wires"></svg>
          <div class="vf-cols">

            <div class="vf-col">
              <div class="vf-group" id="g-partner">
                <div class="vf-gtitle">Sovereign LLM partner</div>
                <div class="vf-gsub">provider-neutral by design — e.g. Mistral, Claude, GPT, open-weight</div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-train" data-component="Training &amp; specialisation">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">Training &amp; specialisation</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">learns from causal, governed, rights-clear Definitions — a corpus / structured context for AI no scrape can produce</div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-infer" data-component="Grounded inference">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">Grounded inference</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">reasons against causal, governed, rights-clear Definitions — a corpus / structured context for AI no RAG can supply</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="vf-gutter"></div>

            <div class="vf-col">
              <div class="vf-group" id="g-poesis">
                <div class="vf-gtitle">Poesis stack</div>
                <div class="vf-gsub">one sovereign instance per organisation — tenant-owned, federal tomorrow</div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-sie" data-component="SIE — Systemic Intelligence Engine">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">SIE — Systemic Intelligence Engine</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">reference implementation of GSM containing Definitions / Ascriptions of the organisation and implementing their governance lifecycle</div>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" data-fold="f-sie">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-sie">
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-definition-manager</b> — hosts GSM, Ascription lifecycle, governance grammar</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-definition-blackboard-manager</b> — Definitions sourcing pipeline</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-operator</b> — executes Norms &amp; Mechanisms: governance evaluation (application of governance, and governance of governance)</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card vf-gate" id="n-itip" data-component="ITIP — domain platform (IT)">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">ITIP — domain platform (IT)</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">serves the <b>PROPOSE / DISPOSE gate to humans</b> — intent, approve, audit, simulate Definitions</div>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" data-fold="f-itip">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-itip">
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip-web-application</b> — the human gate: intent, approval, simulation, appraisal, and audit</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip frameworks</b> — GDPR, NIS2, DORA, AI Act, TOGAF, ISO… standard domain vocabulary / semantics and regulation frameworks that compose GSM Definitions</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip blackboard sourcers</b> — wrap LLMs / agents as KnowledgeSources of Definitions over code repositories, wikis, ticketing tools, online authoritative resources, and other sources</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-saf" data-component="SAFe Agentic Framework">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">SAFe Agentic Framework</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">governed agentic organisation products delivery through deterministic operational gates</div>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" data-fold="f-saf">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-saf">
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>orchestrators</b> — portfolio / program / team</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>specialist bench</b> — architecture, dev, QA, security, docs agents</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>harness</b> — deterministic FSM, artifact &amp; gate checks; humans approve — PROPOSE/DISPOSE applied to delivery</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-detail" id="vf-detail" hidden></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">What a provider gains</p>
      <h2>Beyond the flows.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <div class="card"><h3>A capability edge</h3><p>Not only a compliance one — models grounded in a causal, governed model of the customer's reality, with an evidence-based path to measurable uplift over retrieval-only baselines.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>The missing context layer</h3><p>What turns sovereign models into deployable enterprise systems — able to <em>act</em>, not only answer.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>A clean specialisation corpus</h3><p>Causal, governed, rights-clear traces to tune models on — structural <em>and</em> temporal causality, from the full ascription history.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>A category position</h3><p>The model of choice for the governed causal-context standard Europe is moving toward — named exemplar of an open, vendor-neutral category.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Safe agentic action</h3><p>A deterministic governance layer that makes agentic AI safe to run in banks, public operators, and critical infrastructure.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>A sovereignty narrative</h3><p>Sovereign models grounded in sovereign organisational context, governed by an open, auditable definition standard — EU AI Act, NIS2, DORA ready.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p>
      <h2>Why this is trustworthy enough to scale.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <div class="card"><h3>Model neutrality</h3><p>GSM/SIE is provider-neutral by design — a neutral standard is the one a regulator can endorse.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Evidence over assertion</h3><p>Specialisation and training uplift are proven against strong baselines before they are sold.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Tenant ownership</h3><p>Customer SIE data stays under customer control — legitimacy is the access key, not scale or scraping.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Deterministic disposition</h3><p>Model outputs remain proposals until GSM/SIE validates them. PROPOSE / DISPOSE is the feature, not a limit.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-cta" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Start the conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  #vf { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  #vf .vf-notices { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: .75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-notice {
    margin: 0; border-radius: 10px; padding: .65rem .85rem; font-size: .86rem; color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  #vf .vf-notice-info { background: rgba(56, 189, 248, .08); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, .4); }
  #vf .vf-notice-invariant { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, .10); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, .45); }
  #vf .vf-human {
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 146, 60, .5); background: rgba(251, 146, 60, .08); border-radius: 12px;
    padding: .75rem .9rem; margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-human strong { color: #fb923c; }
  #vf .vf-human ul { margin: .45rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: .84rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  #vf .vf-human li { margin-top: .2rem; }

  #vf .vf-diagram { position: relative; }
  #vf #vf-wires { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; z-index: 2; }
  #vf .vf-cols { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 250px 1fr; z-index: 1; }
  #vf .vf-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-gutter { pointer-events: none; }

  #vf .vf-group {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: .85rem .95rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-gtitle { font-weight: 700; color: #fff; font-size: .98rem; }
  #vf .vf-gsub { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; margin-bottom: .55rem; }

  #vf .vf-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--bg-ink);
    padding: .6rem .75rem; margin-top: .6rem; cursor: pointer; transition: border-color .16s ease, box-shadow .16s ease;
  }
  #vf .vf-card:hover, #vf .vf-card:focus-visible { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(45, 212, 191, .12); outline: none; }
  #vf .vf-card.vf-selected { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(45, 212, 191, .18); }
  #vf .vf-ctitle { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: .89rem; }
  #vf .vf-csub { color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; margin-top: .18rem; }
  #vf .vf-gate { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, .07); border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, .45); }

  #vf .vf-fold-btn {
    margin-top: .5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); background: transparent; color: var(--accent-ink);
    border-radius: 6px; font-size: .74rem; padding: .18rem .55rem; cursor: pointer;
  }
  #vf .vf-fold-btn:hover { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  #vf .vf-fold { display: none; margin-top: .55rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--line-strong); padding-top: .55rem; }
  #vf .vf-fold.open { display: block; }
  #vf .vf-comp {
    font-size: .76rem; color: var(--ink-soft); padding: .3rem .5rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    margin-top: .35rem; background: var(--bg-soft); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
  }
  #vf .vf-comp b { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; color: var(--ink); }

  #vf .vf-flow-hit { pointer-events: stroke; cursor: pointer; }

  #vf .vf-detail {
    margin-top: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--bg-soft); padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-detail h3 { margin: 0 0 .3rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  #vf .vf-dsub { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .87rem; margin-bottom: .85rem; }
  #vf .vf-adherence + .vf-adherence { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-adherence h4 { margin: 0 0 .3rem; font-size: .92rem; }
  #vf .vf-dcols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-dcols h5 { font-size: .78rem; margin: 0 0 .35rem; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }
  #vf .vf-dcols ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .86rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  #vf .vf-dcols li { margin-bottom: .3rem; }
  #vf .vf-comps { margin-top: .9rem; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); }
  #vf .vf-comps b { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .74rem; color: var(--ink); }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    #vf .vf-notices { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #vf .vf-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #vf .vf-gutter { display: none; }
    #vf #vf-wires { display: none; }
    #vf .vf-dcols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const FLOWS = [
    {
      id: 'B1', hex: '#34d399', from: 'n-sie', to: 'n-infer',
      label: 'governed causal context + tools',
      title: 'B1 — Governed causal context & tool surface (Poesis → LLM)',
      sub: 'SIE serves current Definitions, Norms, provenance and causal dependencies into the model — plus a tool surface to retrieve Definitions, inspect Norms, trace Interactions, and validate proposals.',
      partner: ['Capability edge: reasoning against explicit structure, not correlation — follow the why behind the why', 'Measurably fewer unsupported claims vs retrieval-only baselines — proven, not asserted'],
      poesis: ['Answers grounded in what is actually true and governed', 'Model-neutral context standard — any conforming model can plug in'],
      comps: 'Realized by <b>sie-definition-manager</b> (context + tools) consumed by partner inference / MCP surfaces.',
    },
    {
      id: 'B2', hex: '#34d399', from: 'n-infer', to: 'n-itip',
      label: 'proposals → human disposition',
      title: 'B2 — Proposals disposed through the human gate (LLM → Poesis)',
      sub: 'Every model output is a proposal. ITIP serves the PROPOSE/DISPOSE gate to humans; sie-operator executes the norm, schema and provenance checks; every disposition lands in the audit ledger.',
      partner: ['Deployability: agentic action becomes safe to run in banks, public operators, critical infrastructure', 'The compliance story that unlocks regulated European buyers'],
      poesis: ['AI that acts on the organisation\u2019s actual reality — audited, accountable', 'Every disposition enriches the governed record'],
      comps: 'Realized by <b>itip-web-application</b> (human gate) + <b>sie-operator</b> (deterministic evaluation) + audit ledger.',
    },
    {
      id: 'A', hex: '#38bdf8', from: 'n-infer', to: 'n-sie',
      label: 'LLM-backed sourcing of GSM',
      title: 'A — Alimentation: LLMs feed GSM (LLM → Poesis)',
      sub: 'Blackboard sourcers wrap partner models as KnowledgeSources of Definitions over repositories, wikis, ticketing tools, and authoritative online resources. Contributions are confidence-scored (< 1.0) and provenance-stamped; only validated, sealed streams reach the definition manager as asserted Definitions.',
      partner: ['A concrete applied-AI showcase: turning regulation and code into governed, queryable structure', 'R&D feedback loop on extraction, grounding, function calling'],
      poesis: ['Sourcing cost down, coverage up — the fabric fills itself', 'Invariant preserved: LLMs never write governed truth directly'],
      comps: 'Realized by <b>itip blackboard sourcers</b> → <b>sie-definition-blackboard-manager</b> → <b>sie-definition-manager</b>.',
    },
    {
      id: 'C', hex: '#a78bfa', from: 'n-sie', to: 'n-train',
      label: 'evaluation oracle + specialisation corpus',
      title: 'C — Training & specialisation substrate (Poesis → LLM)',
      sub: 'Governed reality scores model answers (evaluation oracle), and the ascription history yields a causal corpus in two dimensions — structural (mechanisms, interactions) and temporal (time-stamped ascriptions).',
      partner: ['A uniquely clean specialisation corpus: causal, governed, rights-clear — a durable moat', 'Benchmarks against strong baselines: evidence over assertion'],
      poesis: ['Specialised sovereign models raise inference and sourcing quality — compounding every other flow', 'Legitimacy-gated access: tenant ownership absolute'],
      comps: 'Realized by <b>sie-operator</b> (evaluation) + <b>sie-definition-manager</b> (corpus) under explicit contractual and consent boundaries.',
    },
    {
      id: 'D', hex: '#94a3b8', from: 'n-infer', to: 'n-saf', dashed: true,
      label: 'agent bench builds the stack',
      title: 'D — Agentic delivery: LLM agents build Poesis itself (LLM → Poesis)',
      sub: 'Partner models power the SAFe Agentic Framework\u2019s orchestrators and specialist bench. Agent teams deliver SIE and ITIP through deterministic harness gates with human approval — the same PROPOSE/DISPOSE invariant applied to software delivery.',
      partner: ['A living reference of governed multi-agent engineering on partner models', 'Dogfooding evidence for the enterprise agentic story'],
      poesis: ['Velocity: the stack is built by the very pattern it sells', 'Delivery traces are themselves governed, auditable artifacts'],
      comps: 'Realized by the <b>SAFe Agentic Framework</b> (orchestration layers, actor bench, deterministic harness) targeting the SIE/ITIP repos.',
    },
  ];

  const svg = document.getElementById('vf-wires');
  const diagram = document.getElementById('vf-diagram');
  const detail = document.getElementById('vf-detail');
  let selectedFlow = null;
  let selectedComponent = null;

  function anchor(el, side) {
    const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
    const d = diagram.getBoundingClientRect();
    return { x: (side === 'right' ? r.right : r.left) - d.left, y: r.top + r.height / 2 - d.top };
  }

  function draw() {
    if (!svg || !diagram) return;
    svg.innerHTML = '';
    if (window.innerWidth <= 860) return;
    svg.setAttribute('width', String(diagram.clientWidth));
    svg.setAttribute('height', String(diagram.clientHeight));

    FLOWS.forEach((f) => {
      const fromEl = document.getElementById(f.from);
      const toEl = document.getElementById(f.to);
      if (!fromEl || !toEl) return;
      const a = anchor(fromEl, fromEl.closest('#g-partner') ? 'right' : 'left');
      const b = anchor(toEl, toEl.closest('#g-partner') ? 'right' : 'left');
      const midX = (a.x + b.x) / 2;
      const related = selectedComponent && (f.from === selectedComponent || f.to === selectedComponent);
      const sel = selectedFlow === f.id || related;

      const pathData = `M ${a.x} ${a.y} C ${midX} ${a.y}, ${midX} ${b.y}, ${b.x} ${b.y}`;

      const hit = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'path');
      hit.setAttribute('d', pathData);
      hit.setAttribute('fill', 'none');
      hit.setAttribute('stroke', 'transparent');
      hit.setAttribute('stroke-width', '20');
      hit.setAttribute('class', 'vf-flow-hit');
      hit.setAttribute('aria-label', f.title);
      hit.addEventListener('click', () => selectFlow(f.id));
      svg.appendChild(hit);

      const p = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'path');
      p.setAttribute('d', pathData);
      p.setAttribute('fill', 'none');
      p.setAttribute('stroke', f.hex);
      p.setAttribute('stroke-width', sel ? '7' : '5');
      p.setAttribute('opacity', (selectedFlow || selectedComponent) && !sel ? '0.16' : '0.82');
      p.setAttribute('pointer-events', 'none');
      if (f.dashed) p.setAttribute('stroke-dasharray', '6 5');
      svg.appendChild(p);

      const tip = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'circle');
      tip.setAttribute('cx', String(b.x));
      tip.setAttribute('cy', String(b.y));
      tip.setAttribute('r', sel ? '6' : '5');
      tip.setAttribute('fill', f.hex);
      tip.setAttribute('opacity', (selectedFlow || selectedComponent) && !sel ? '0.16' : '1');
      tip.setAttribute('pointer-events', 'none');
      svg.appendChild(tip);
    });
  }

  function adherenceMarkup(flow) {
    return `<article class="vf-adherence">
      <h4 style="color:${flow.hex}">${flow.title}</h4>
      <p class="vf-dsub">${flow.sub}</p>
      <div class="vf-dcols">
        <div><h5>Value for the LLM partner</h5><ul>${flow.partner.map((value) => `<li>${value}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>
        <div><h5>Value for Poesis / the customer</h5><ul>${flow.poesis.map((value) => `<li>${value}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vf-comps">Adherence locus — ${flow.comps}</div>
    </article>`;
  }

  function showAdherences(title, flows) {
    if (!detail) return;
    detail.hidden = false;
    detail.innerHTML = `<h3>${title}</h3>${flows.map(adherenceMarkup).join('')}`;
    draw();
    detail.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
  }

  function clearSelection() {
    selectedFlow = null;
    selectedComponent = null;
    document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card').forEach((card) => card.classList.remove('vf-selected'));
    if (detail) detail.hidden = true;
    draw();
  }

  function selectFlow(id) {
    if (selectedFlow === id && !selectedComponent) {
      clearSelection();
      return;
    }
    selectedFlow = id;
    selectedComponent = null;
    document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card').forEach((card) => card.classList.remove('vf-selected'));
    const flow = FLOWS.find((candidate) => candidate.id === id);
    showAdherences(`Selected value flow — ${flow.label}`, [flow]);
  }

  function selectComponent(card) {
    if (selectedComponent === card.id && !selectedFlow) {
      clearSelection();
      return;
    }
    selectedComponent = card.id;
    selectedFlow = null;
    document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card').forEach((candidate) => candidate.classList.toggle('vf-selected', candidate === card));
    const flows = FLOWS.filter((flow) => flow.from === card.id || flow.to === card.id);
    showAdherences(`${card.dataset.component} — ${flows.length} connected adherence${flows.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`, flows);
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card[data-component]').forEach((card) => {
    card.setAttribute('role', 'button');
    card.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
    card.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      if (event.target.closest('.vf-fold-btn')) return;
      selectComponent(card);
    });
    card.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      if (event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' ') {
        event.preventDefault();
        selectComponent(card);
      }
    });
  });

  document.querySelectorAll('.vf-fold-btn').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      event.stopPropagation();
      const fold = document.getElementById(btn.dataset.fold);
      if (!fold) return;
      fold.classList.toggle('open');
      btn.textContent = `${fold.classList.contains('open') ? '▾' : '▸'} components`;
      draw();
    });
  });

  window.addEventListener('resize', draw);
  draw();
</script>
